       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum recommended metformin dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **850 mg twice daily** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, divided in some other way\n- Another dose entirely\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
